      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "[codex] Prevent stale review comment sync overwrites",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- Prevent stale apply/comment-sync runs from overwriting a newer durable ClawSweeper review comment.\n- Trust only pull-request review comments that are bot-owned, have the durable review marker as the final footer, and expose a trailing automation verdict marker with a newer `reviewed_at`.\n- Add regression coverage for the real overwrite race plus untrusted/user-authored markers, forged marker prose, forged review footers, and issue comments.\n\n## Root cause\n\nA long-running apply/comment-sync job could load older state and later PATCH the durable review comment after a newer exact-review run had already updated it. Because the sync path compared desired body/hash metadata but did not check live review freshness, it could roll the public comment from a newer review back to an older one.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `pnpm run build`\n- `pnpm exec node --test test/clawsweeper.test.ts`\n- `pnpm run format:check`\n- `autoreview --mode local --codex-bin /root/.nvm/versions/node/v22.21.1/lib/node_modules/@openai/codex/node_modules/@openai/codex-linux-x64/vendor/x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/bin/codex ...`\n\n## Autoreview\n\nCodex autoreview initially found trust-boundary issues in the freshness parser. Accepted and fixed:\n\n- Do not trust user-authored marker comments.\n- Do not trust marker-shaped text in generated review prose.\n- Do not apply PR verdict-tail freshness logic to issue comments.\n- Require the durable `clawsweeper-review` marker to be the final footer before trusting the preceding verdict marker.\n\nFinal autoreview result: `autoreview clean: no accepted/actionable findings reported`.\n",
        "branch": "feature/clawsweeper-stale-comment-sync-guard",
